questions.question_text:
In a certain code:
'P + Q' means 'P is the father of Q';
'P − Q' means 'P is the sister of Q';
'P × Q' means 'P is the wife of Q';
'P ÷ Q' means 'P is the son of Q'.

If 'M ÷ N × O + P − Q', how is M related to Q?

In a certain code:
'A @ B' means 'A is the mother of B';
'A # B' means 'A is the brother of B';
'A $ B' means 'A is the husband of B';
'A & B' means 'A is the daughter of B'.

In the expression 'K # L & M $ N @ O', how is N related to K?

In a certain code:
'A ★ B' means 'A is the father of B';
'A ● B' means 'A is the sister of B';
'A ▲ B' means 'A is the wife of B';
'A ◆ B' means 'A is the son of B';
'A ■ B' means 'A is the mother of B'.

Given that 'G ★ H ● I', 'J ▲ G', 'K ■ J' and 'I ◆ J' are all true, how is I related to K?

In a certain code:
'A # B' means 'A is 3 m north of B';
'A $ B' means 'A is 4 m east of B';
'A @ B' means 'A is 3 m south of B';
'A % B' means 'A is 4 m west of B'.

If 'P # Q', 'R $ Q', 'S @ R' and 'T % S', what is the shortest distance between R and T, and in which direction is R with respect to T?
